---
import Layout from '../layouts/Layout.astro';
import MarketingNav from '../components/MarketingNav';
import MarketingFooter from '../components/MarketingFooter';

const p = 'text-sm text-gray-700 mb-3 last:mb-0 leading-relaxed';
const ul = 'list-disc pl-5 text-sm text-gray-700 mb-3 space-y-1';
const h3 = 'text-base font-semibold text-gray-900 mt-5 mb-2';
const h2 = 'text-xl font-bold text-gray-900 pt-4 mb-4';
---

<Layout
  title="Privacy Policy | HoursServed"
  description="HoursServed privacy policy — how we collect, use, and protect personal information for volunteer organizations."
>
  <div class="min-h-screen bg-slate-50">
    <MarketingNav client:load />

    <!-- Hero -->
    <div class="bg-slate-900 text-white py-16 px-4 text-center relative overflow-hidden">
      <div class="absolute inset-0 pointer-events-none" style="background: radial-gradient(ellipse 80% 60% at 50% 120%, rgba(20,184,166,.18) 0%, transparent 70%)"></div>
      <span class="inline-block text-xs font-semibold tracking-widest uppercase text-teal-400 border border-teal-500/40 rounded-full px-4 py-1 mb-5">Legal</span>
      <h1 class="text-4xl font-bold mb-3">Privacy Policy</h1>
      <p class="text-slate-400 text-sm max-w-md mx-auto">How we collect, use, and protect your personal information.</p>
      <div class="flex gap-8 justify-center flex-wrap mt-6 text-xs text-slate-500">
        <span><strong class="text-slate-300 font-medium">Effective Date:</strong> May 15, 2026</span>
        <span><strong class="text-slate-300 font-medium">Last Updated:</strong> May 18, 2026</span>
      </div>
    </div>

    <!-- Layout -->
    <div class="max-w-6xl mx-auto px-4 py-10">

      <!-- Content -->
      <main class="max-w-4xl mx-auto">

        <!-- Section 1 -->
        <div id="who-we-are" class="bg-white border border-gray-200 rounded-xl p-8 mb-4 shadow-sm scroll-mt-24">
          <h2 class={h2}>1. Who We Are</h2>
          <p class={p}>HoursServed.com is operated by Abacus Media Marketing Inc., a corporation incorporated under the Canada Business Corporations Act. We provide a web-based service administration platform designed for volunteer organizations, primarily Lions Clubs and similar service clubs, to manage members, track service hours, organize events, and submit reports to Lions Clubs International.</p>
          <p class={p}>In this Privacy Policy, "HoursServed", "we", "us", and "our" refer to Abacus Media Marketing Inc. and the HoursServed.com platform.</p>
          <ul class={ul}>
            <li><strong>Company:</strong> Abacus Media Marketing Inc.</li>
            <li><strong>Platform:</strong> HoursServed.com</li>
            <li><strong>Email:</strong> <a href="mailto:support@hoursserved.com" class="text-blue-600 hover:underline">support@hoursserved.com</a></li>
            <li><strong>Country of incorporation:</strong> Canada</li>
          </ul>
        </div>

        <!-- Section 2 -->
        <div id="scope" class="bg-white border border-gray-200 rounded-xl p-8 mb-4 shadow-sm scroll-mt-24">
          <h2 class={h2}>2. Scope</h2>
          <p class={p}>This policy applies to:</p>
          <ul class={ul}>
            <li>Club secretaries, officers, and administrators who create and manage a HoursServed account</li>
            <li>Club members whose information is entered by their club secretary</li>
            <li>Volunteers entered by their club</li>
            <li>Visitors to hoursserved.com</li>
            <li>District administrators who access the District Dashboard</li>
          </ul>
          <p class={p}>This policy does not apply to third-party services including the Lions Clubs International myLCI portal, Google Calendar, Stripe, or Apify.</p>
        </div>

        <!-- Section 3 -->
        <div id="information-we-collect" class="bg-white border border-gray-200 rounded-xl p-8 mb-4 shadow-sm scroll-mt-24">
          <h2 class={h2}>3. Information We Collect</h2>

          <h3 class={h3}>3.1 Information You Provide Directly</h3>
          <ul class={ul}>
            <li>Name and email address</li>
            <li>Club name, district code, and Lions International club number</li>
            <li>Club Settings including venue defaults and reporting preferences</li>
            <li>Payment information processed through Stripe</li>
          </ul>

          <h3 class={h3}>3.2 Member and Volunteer Information</h3>
          <ul class={ul}>
            <li>First name, last name, email address</li>
            <li>Phone number and mailing address (optional)</li>
            <li>Member role and officer status</li>
            <li>RSVP responses, attendance records, and service hours</li>
            <li>Dues payment status</li>
          </ul>
          <p class={p}><strong>Note:</strong> Club secretaries are responsible for ensuring they have appropriate authority to enter member information. By entering member data, the club secretary represents they have consent or legitimate authority to do so.</p>

          <h3 class={h3}>3.3 Event and Service Data</h3>
          <ul class={ul}>
            <li>Event names, dates, times, locations, and types</li>
            <li>Lions International reporting fields including venue, cause, people served, and activity level</li>
            <li>Monthly report data submitted to myLCI</li>
            <li>Shift management data</li>
          </ul>

          <h3 class={h3}>3.4 Automatically Collected</h3>
          <ul class={ul}>
            <li>IP address and approximate location</li>
            <li>Browser type and device information</li>
            <li>Pages visited and features used</li>
            <li>Date and time of access</li>
            <li>Email delivery and open status</li>
          </ul>

          <h3 class={h3}>3.5 Cookies</h3>
          <p class={p}>We use cookies for login sessions, preferences, and usage analytics. See our <a href="/cookie-policy/" class="text-blue-600 hover:underline">Cookie Policy</a> for details.</p>
        </div>

        <!-- Section 4 -->
        <div id="how-we-use" class="bg-white border border-gray-200 rounded-xl p-8 mb-4 shadow-sm scroll-mt-24">
          <h2 class={h2}>4. How We Use Your Information</h2>

          <p class={p}><strong>To provide the service:</strong> create and manage club accounts, send invitations and nudges, track attendance and service hours, generate monthly reports, automate myLCI submissions, process payments, and provide District Dashboard access.</p>
          <p class={p}><strong>To improve the service:</strong> analyze feature usage, identify and fix issues, and develop new features.</p>
          <p class={p}><strong>To communicate:</strong> account notifications and receipts, support responses, and product updates (unsubscribe anytime).</p>
          <p class={p}><strong>To comply with legal obligations:</strong> respond to lawful government requests, meet privacy legislation requirements, and maintain legally required records.</p>
        </div>

        <!-- Section 5 -->
        <div id="legal-basis" class="bg-white border border-gray-200 rounded-xl p-8 mb-4 shadow-sm scroll-mt-24">
          <h2 class={h2}>5. Legal Basis for Processing</h2>

          <h3 class={h3}>5.1 UK and EU Users — UK GDPR and EU GDPR</h3>
          <p class={p}>Where the UK or EU GDPR applies, we rely on the following lawful bases:</p>
          <ul class={ul}>
            <li>Legitimate interests, for business-to-business outreach to the named officers of service clubs whose role includes club administration and reporting. You may object to this processing at any time.</li>
            <li>Performance of a contract, to provide the HoursServed service to account holders.</li>
            <li>Consent, where required, which you may withdraw at any time.</li>
            <li>Legal obligation, where we must process your information to comply with applicable law.</li>
          </ul>

          <h3 class={h3}>5.2 Canadian Users — PIPEDA and Quebec Law 25</h3>
          <p class={p}>We rely on consent or where permitted by law. Club secretaries consent on behalf of their organization.</p>

          <h3 class={h3}>5.3 US Users</h3>
          <p class={p}>Processing is necessary to provide contracted service and for legitimate business interests. California residents have additional CCPA rights as described in Section 8.3.</p>

          <h3 class={h3}>5.4 Australian Users</h3>
          <p class={p}>We operate in accordance with the Privacy Act 1988 and the 13 Australian Privacy Principles. Information is collected only for purposes directly related to providing HoursServed.</p>
        </div>

        <!-- Section 6 -->
        <div id="how-we-share" class="bg-white border border-gray-200 rounded-xl p-8 mb-4 shadow-sm scroll-mt-24">
          <h2 class={h2}>6. How We Share Your Information</h2>

          <p class={p}><strong>6.1</strong> We do not sell, rent, or trade personal information. HoursServed is advertisement-free.</p>
          <p class={p}><strong>6.2 Service providers:</strong> Base44 (application platform), Vercel (web hosting), Stripe (payments), Supabase (backend infrastructure), Apify (myLCI automation), Google (calendar sync). All are contractually required to protect data.</p>
          <p class={p}><strong>6.3 Lions Clubs International:</strong> The myLCI AutoSubmit feature submits your report data at your explicit direction using credentials you provide.</p>
          <p class={p}><strong>6.4 District administrators</strong> can see club reporting status, event activity, and aggregate service hours. Individual member contact details are not shared with district administrators.</p>
          <p class={p}><strong>6.5 Legal requirements:</strong> We may disclose data if required by law, court order, or government authority.</p>
          <p class={p}><strong>6.6 Business transfers:</strong> Data may transfer in an acquisition or merger, with advance notice to users.</p>
        </div>

        <!-- Section 7 -->
        <div id="data-retention" class="bg-white border border-gray-200 rounded-xl p-8 mb-4 shadow-sm scroll-mt-24">
          <h2 class={h2}>7. Data Retention</h2>
          <p class={p}>We keep personal information only as long as necessary for the purposes for which it was collected. Contact data for prospects who do not respond to our outreach is deleted within 6 to 12 months of the last contact. Account data is retained for the life of the account and, after closure, only for the period required to meet our legal, tax, and accounting obligations, after which it is securely deleted or anonymized.</p>
          <ul class={ul}>
            <li>Active account data: retained for the duration of your subscription</li>
            <li>Member and volunteer records: deleted within 90 days of cancellation on request</li>
            <li>Service hour and attendance records: retained 7 years</li>
            <li>Payment records: per applicable tax law</li>
            <li>Email logs: 12 months</li>
            <li>System logs: 24 months</li>
          </ul>
        </div>

        <!-- Section 8 -->
        <div id="privacy-rights" class="bg-white border border-gray-200 rounded-xl p-8 mb-4 shadow-sm scroll-mt-24">
          <h2 class={h2}>8. Your Privacy Rights</h2>

          <h3 class={h3}>8.1 All Users</h3>
          <p class={p}>Subject to applicable law, you may request access to, correction of, or deletion of your personal information; object to or restrict its processing; withdraw consent; and request a copy of your information in a portable format. Quebec residents may also request de-indexing of information in certain circumstances. To exercise any right, contact our Privacy Officer at <a href="mailto:support@hoursserved.com" class="text-blue-600 hover:underline">support@hoursserved.com</a>. We respond within the time limits set by applicable law.</p>

          <h3 class={h3}>8.2 UK and EU Users (UK GDPR / EU GDPR)</h3>
          <p class={p}>You additionally have the right to restriction, objection, and to withdraw consent. To lodge a complaint: UK residents may contact the ICO at <a href="https://ico.org.uk" class="text-blue-600 hover:underline">ico.org.uk</a>; EU residents may contact their national data protection authority.</p>

          <h3 class={h3}>8.3 California Users (CCPA)</h3>
          <p class={p}>You have the right to know what data is collected, to delete personal information, and to opt out of sale (note: HoursServed does not sell data). You are protected from discrimination for exercising these rights. Submit requests to <a href="mailto:support@hoursserved.com" class="text-blue-600 hover:underline">support@hoursserved.com</a> with "CCPA Request" in the subject. We will respond within 45 days.</p>

          <h3 class={h3}>8.4 Canadian Users (PIPEDA and Quebec Law 25)</h3>
          <p class={p}>You have the right to access, challenge accuracy, and withdraw consent. Lodge complaints with the Office of the Privacy Commissioner at <a href="https://priv.gc.ca" class="text-blue-600 hover:underline">priv.gc.ca</a>. Quebec residents additionally have the right to data portability, the right to be informed of automated decisions, and the right to object. Privacy Officer: <a href="mailto:support@hoursserved.com" class="text-blue-600 hover:underline">support@hoursserved.com</a>.</p>

          <h3 class={h3}>8.5 Australian Users (Privacy Act 1988)</h3>
          <p class={p}>You have the right to access and correct your personal information, and to lodge a complaint with the OAIC at <a href="https://oaic.gov.au" class="text-blue-600 hover:underline">oaic.gov.au</a>.</p>
        </div>

        <!-- Section 9 -->
        <div id="data-security" class="bg-white border border-gray-200 rounded-xl p-8 mb-4 shadow-sm scroll-mt-24">
          <h2 class={h2}>9. Data Security</h2>
          <p class={p}>Our security measures include:</p>
          <ul class={ul}>
            <li>TLS encryption in transit</li>
            <li>Role-based access controls</li>
            <li>Encrypted secrets management for myLCI credentials</li>
            <li>Regular security reviews</li>
            <li>Automated daily backups</li>
          </ul>
          <p class={p}>No method of electronic transmission or storage is 100% secure. Data breach notification will be provided as required by applicable law.</p>
        </div>

        <!-- Section 10 -->
        <div id="international-transfers" class="bg-white border border-gray-200 rounded-xl p-8 mb-4 shadow-sm scroll-mt-24">
          <h2 class={h2}>10. International Data Transfers</h2>
          <p class={p}>We use service providers located outside Canada, including in the United States, to operate HoursServed. Where we transfer personal information outside your jurisdiction, including outside Quebec, the UK, or the EU, we do so under appropriate safeguards such as standard contractual clauses or the UK International Data Transfer Agreement. Australian users consent to international transfer by using the service. A list of our subprocessors and links to their data processing agreements is available at <a href="https://hoursserved.com/legal/processors" class="text-blue-600 hover:underline">hoursserved.com/legal/processors</a>.</p>
        </div>

        <!-- Section 11 -->
        <div id="childrens-privacy" class="bg-white border border-gray-200 rounded-xl p-8 mb-4 shadow-sm scroll-mt-24">
          <h2 class={h2}>11. Children's Privacy</h2>
          <p class={p}>HoursServed is intended for adults. We do not knowingly collect information from individuals under 18. If you believe we have inadvertently collected data from a minor, please contact us at <a href="mailto:support@hoursserved.com" class="text-blue-600 hover:underline">support@hoursserved.com</a> and we will delete it promptly.</p>
        </div>

        <!-- Section 12 -->
        <div id="third-party-links" class="bg-white border border-gray-200 rounded-xl p-8 mb-4 shadow-sm scroll-mt-24">
          <h2 class={h2}>12. Third-Party Links</h2>
          <p class={p}>Our platform may contain links to third-party websites or services. We are not responsible for the privacy practices of those third parties. We encourage you to review their privacy policies independently.</p>
        </div>

        <!-- Section 13 -->
        <div id="regional-rights" class="bg-white border border-gray-200 rounded-xl p-8 mb-4 shadow-sm scroll-mt-24">
          <h2 class={h2}>13. Do Other Regions Have Specific Privacy Rights?</h2>

          <h3 class={h3}>United Kingdom</h3>
          <p class={p}>If you are located in the United Kingdom, the UK General Data Protection Regulation (UK GDPR) and the Data Protection Act 2018 apply to our processing of your personal information.</p>
          <p class={p}>You have the following rights under UK GDPR:</p>
          <ul class={ul}>
            <li>The right to access your personal data</li>
            <li>The right to rectification of inaccurate data</li>
            <li>The right to erasure ('right to be forgotten')</li>
            <li>The right to restriction of processing</li>
            <li>The right to data portability</li>
            <li>The right to object to processing</li>
            <li>Rights in relation to automated decision making</li>
          </ul>
          <p class={p}>To exercise any of these rights, contact our Privacy Officer at <a href="mailto:support@hoursserved.com" class="text-blue-600 hover:underline">support@hoursserved.com</a>.</p>
          <p class={p}>If you are not satisfied with our response, you have the right to lodge a complaint with the Information Commissioner's Office (ICO), the UK supervisory authority for data protection issues. Website: <a href="https://ico.org.uk" class="text-blue-600 hover:underline">ico.org.uk</a> | Telephone: 0303 123 1113</p>

          <h3 class={h3}>Quebec, Canada (Law 25 / Bill 64)</h3>
          <p class={p}>If you are located in Quebec, Canada, the Act Respecting the Protection of Personal Information in the Private Sector (Law 25, also known as Bill 64), as amended effective September 2023, applies to our processing of your personal information.</p>
          <p class={p}><strong>Privacy Officer:</strong> Abacus Media Marketing Inc. has designated a Privacy Officer responsible for the protection of personal information. See Section 17 for complete Privacy Officer contact details.</p>
          <p class={p}>Your rights under Law 25 include:</p>
          <ul class={ul}>
            <li>The right to access your personal information</li>
            <li>The right to rectification of inaccurate information</li>
            <li>The right to data portability (where applicable)</li>
            <li>The right to withdraw consent at any time</li>
            <li>The right to be informed of any privacy incident affecting your information</li>
          </ul>
          <p class={p}><strong>Privacy Impact Assessments:</strong> We conduct Privacy Impact Assessments (PIAs) for any new technology project that involves the collection, use, or disclosure of personal information, as required by Law 25.</p>
          <p class={p}>If you have concerns about how we handle your personal information, you may contact the Commission d'accès à l'information (CAI), Quebec's data protection authority. Website: <a href="https://cai.quebec.ca" class="text-blue-600 hover:underline">cai.quebec.ca</a> | Telephone: 1-888-528-7741</p>

          <h3 class={h3}>Australia and New Zealand</h3>
          <p class={p}>If you are located in Australia, your personal information is handled in accordance with the Privacy Act 1988 (Cth) and the 13 Australian Privacy Principles (APPs). If you have a complaint about our handling of your personal information, you may contact the Office of the Australian Information Commissioner (OAIC) at <a href="https://oaic.gov.au" class="text-blue-600 hover:underline">oaic.gov.au</a> or by calling 1300 363 992.</p>
          <p class={p}>If you are located in New Zealand, your personal information is handled in accordance with the Privacy Act 2020. If you have a complaint, you may contact the Office of the Privacy Commissioner (OPC) at <a href="https://privacy.org.nz" class="text-blue-600 hover:underline">privacy.org.nz</a>.</p>

          <h3 class={h3}>Republic of South Africa</h3>
          <p class={p}>If you are located in the Republic of South Africa, the Protection of Personal Information Act 4 of 2013 (POPIA) applies to our processing of your personal information. You have the right to access, correct, and object to the processing of your personal information. If you have a complaint, you may contact the Information Regulator (South Africa) at <a href="https://inforegulator.org.za" class="text-blue-600 hover:underline">inforegulator.org.za</a>.</p>
        </div>

        <!-- Section 14 -->
        <div id="changes-to-policy" class="bg-white border border-gray-200 rounded-xl p-8 mb-4 shadow-sm scroll-mt-24">
          <h2 class={h2}>14. Changes to This Policy</h2>
          <p class={p}>We will communicate material changes by updating the Last Updated date at the top of this page, displaying an in-app notice, and emailing the primary club contact. Continued use of HoursServed after changes are posted constitutes acceptance of the updated policy.</p>
        </div>

        <!-- Section 15 -->
        <div id="exercise-rights" class="bg-white border border-gray-200 rounded-xl p-8 mb-4 shadow-sm scroll-mt-24">
          <h2 class={h2}>15. How to Exercise Your Rights</h2>
          <ul class={ul}>
            <li><strong>Email:</strong> <a href="mailto:support@hoursserved.com" class="text-blue-600 hover:underline">support@hoursserved.com</a></li>
            <li><strong>Subject line:</strong> Privacy Request — [your country]</li>
            <li><strong>Include:</strong> your name, email address, club name, and a description of your request</li>
          </ul>
          <p class={p}>We will respond within 30 days. Identity verification may be required. There is no fee for reasonable requests.</p>
        </div>

        <!-- Section 16 -->
        <div id="jurisdiction-disclosures" class="bg-white border border-gray-200 rounded-xl p-8 mb-4 shadow-sm scroll-mt-24">
          <h2 class={h2}>16. Jurisdiction-Specific Disclosures</h2>

          <h3 class={h3}>16.1 Canada — PIPEDA</h3>
          <p class={p}>We collect, use, and disclose personal information in accordance with PIPEDA. You may withdraw consent at any time, subject to legal restrictions, by contacting <a href="mailto:support@hoursserved.com" class="text-blue-600 hover:underline">support@hoursserved.com</a>.</p>

          <h3 class={h3}>16.2 Quebec — Law 25</h3>
          <p class={p}>Our Privacy Officer is reachable at <a href="mailto:support@hoursserved.com" class="text-blue-600 hover:underline">support@hoursserved.com</a>. A Privacy Impact Assessment is conducted prior to any new collection presenting privacy risk.</p>

          <h3 class={h3}>16.3 UK — UK GDPR</h3>
          <p class={p}>Personal data is processed in accordance with the UK GDPR and the Data Protection Act 2018. You may lodge complaints with the Information Commissioner's Office (ICO) at <a href="https://ico.org.uk" class="text-blue-600 hover:underline">ico.org.uk</a> or by calling 0303 123 1113.</p>

          <h3 class={h3}>16.4 EU — EU GDPR</h3>
          <p class={p}>Personal data is processed in accordance with the EU General Data Protection Regulation (GDPR). You may lodge complaints with the data protection authority in your EU member state.</p>

          <h3 class={h3}>16.5 Australia — Privacy Act 1988</h3>
          <p class={p}>Personal information is handled in accordance with the Privacy Act 1988 and the 13 Australian Privacy Principles. You may lodge a complaint with the Office of the Australian Information Commissioner (OAIC) at <a href="https://oaic.gov.au" class="text-blue-600 hover:underline">oaic.gov.au</a> or by calling 1300 363 992.</p>

          <h3 class={h3}>16.6 USA — State Privacy Laws</h3>
          <p class={p}>HoursServed does not sell personal information and does not engage in targeted advertising. California residents have the rights described in Section 8.3. Residents of Virginia, Colorado, Connecticut, and Texas have similar rights under their respective state laws — contact us at <a href="mailto:support@hoursserved.com" class="text-blue-600 hover:underline">support@hoursserved.com</a> to exercise them.</p>
        </div>

        <!-- Section 17 -->
        <div id="privacy-officer" class="bg-white border border-gray-200 rounded-xl p-8 mb-4 shadow-sm scroll-mt-24">
          <h2 class={h2}>17. Person in Charge of the Protection of Personal Information</h2>
          <p class={p}>Abacus Media Marketing Inc., operator of HoursServed.com, has designated a Privacy Officer responsible for the protection of personal information and for compliance with applicable privacy law, including Quebec's Law 25 and the UK GDPR.</p>
          <ul class={ul}>
            <li><strong>Privacy Officer:</strong> Steve Wetmore</li>
            <li><strong>Title:</strong> Privacy Officer, Abacus Media Marketing Inc.</li>
            <li><strong>Email:</strong> <a href="mailto:support@hoursserved.com" class="text-blue-600 hover:underline">support@hoursserved.com</a></li>
            <li><strong>Mail:</strong> 88 Bloor St E, Suite 1506, Toronto, ON M4W 3G9, Canada</li>
          </ul>
          <p class={p}>The Privacy Officer handles access, correction, objection, erasure, and data-portability requests, oversees breach notification, and conducts privacy impact assessments.</p>
          <p class={p}>If you are not satisfied with our response, you may contact the relevant regulator:</p>
          <ul class={ul}>
            <li>Quebec residents: Commission d'accès à l'information du Québec (CAI)</li>
            <li>UK residents: Information Commissioner's Office (ICO)</li>
          </ul>

          <h3 class={h3}>Accountability Records</h3>
          <p class={p}>Our Legitimate Interests Assessment and Privacy Impact Assessment are available to supervisory authorities and data subjects on request by contacting <a href="mailto:support@hoursserved.com" class="text-blue-600 hover:underline">support@hoursserved.com</a>.</p>

          <p class="text-xs text-gray-400 border-t border-gray-100 pt-6 mt-8">
            This Privacy Policy has been prepared in good faith covering our current and intended markets. It has not been reviewed by qualified legal counsel. HoursServed recommends engaging a privacy lawyer for formal review when revenue permits. Effective May 15, 2026.
          </p>
        </div>

      </main>
    </div>

    <MarketingFooter />
  </div>
</Layout>
